--- make
description: A typed request body in requests/: a controller parameter typed with it only sees data of that shape
category: Routes and APIs
usage: <Name> [--fields "name: string, age?: int"]
--fields: The fields, comma separated, as name: type (? for optional, = for a default). Default: name: string
example: kscript make request NewPerson --fields "name: string, age?: int, role?: string"
example: kscript make request orders/NewOrder --fields "product: string, quantity: int = 1"
to: {{ paths.requests }}/{{ dir }}{{ kebab }}{{ ext }}
hint: Use it in a controller: import "../{{ paths.requests }}/{{ dir }}{{ kebab }}{{ ext }}", then fn store(json: {{ pascal }}). A body that doesn't fit gets 422.
---
/// The body of a {{ title }} request. Data that doesn't fit is answered with 422 before the controller runs.
type {{ pascal }} {
{{#each fields}}
  {{ item }}
{{else}}
  name: string
{{/each}}
}
